# Frames the fake device must receive for e2e_7105.script, in order.
# "<to> <opcode> [args...]": SW = switcher socket, HIS = streaming module.
SW FF              # discovery (type 0x81) via --probe
SW 49              # panel opens: read full state
SW 80 03           # PGM 3
SW 81 04           # PVW 4
SW 83              # CUT
SW 84              # AUTO
SW B1 02           # RATE 3
SW 8E              # FADE
SW 8F              # UP = SET_WIPE ...
SW 92 25           # ... + wipe style 0x25
SW 8F              # LEFT
SW 92 23
SW 8F              # RIGHT
SW 92 27
SW 8F              # DOWN
SW 92 29
SW 8D              # MIX transition
SW CC              # AFV button
SW CB              # MIX button
SW B9 04           # CH1 source = IN2 (device code 4)
SW CE 37           # CH1 volume 50 -> 55
SW D0              # F2
SW D4              # F3
SW D6              # F7
SW 85              # FTB
SW 49              # DS
SW A3 0B           # F1: PGM Out = 1080P50
SW CD              # STILL
SW 86 01           # PIP on
SW A2 02           # PIP size Large
SW A0 0A 00        # PIP H = 10
SW A0 14 00        # PIP H = 20
SW 9F 03           # PIP border width 3
SW 86 00           # PIP off
HIS 24             # read streaming module IP info
HIS 23 08 08 08 08 02 50 3B 8C   # set DNS 8.8.8.8 (+ constant tail)
HIS 6A 00          # read URL index 0 (shown as "1")
HIS 67 00 00 04    # set URL: 67 00 idx=0 name_len=4 ("main")
SW 49              # DS
SW FF @time        # Sync time: 27-byte frame, BCD = simulator's clock
SW FF              # RETURN: back to search, rescan (unicast probe)
SW FF              # Probe button
SW 49              # Connect by IP: panel opens and reads state
